  "statement": "The number\n\n\\[\\frac{9^{9} - 8^{8}}{1001}\\]\n\nis an integer. Compute the sum of its prime factors.",
  "answerChoices": [],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "231",
    "value": "231"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-guts-2025-p7.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Observe\n\n\\[{9^{9}-8^{8}=27^{6}-16^{6}}\\] \\[{=(27^{2}-16^{2})(27^{4}+27^{2}\\cdot16^{2}+16^{4})}\\] \\[{=(27-16)(27+16)(27^{2}-27\\cdot16+16^{2})(27^{2}+27\\cdot16+16^{2})}\\] \\[{=11\\cdot43\\cdot553\\cdot1417.}\\]\n\nThe remaining factorizations are motivated by the fact that \\(1001 = 7\\cdot 11\\cdot 13\\) . We see that \\(553 = 7\\cdot 79\\) and \\(1417 = 13\\cdot 109\\) , so the answer is \\(43 + 79 + 109 = \\boxed {231}\\) .",
